Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||10-08-2001||01:40 PM||||I knew my starter was going, I was going to take care of it shortly but now it died on me!<P>#@$*<P>I tried to start it but it was cranking over really slowly.  It is not the battery that is weak.  Something in the starter must be shot!<BR>*EDIT*  The engine was warm.  I'll try it again 15 minutes later when its cool.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||10-08-2001||02:19 PM||||Disconnect the battery and then check the connections on the starter first.  Could be a loose, frayed or corroded wire.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||10-08-2001||02:55 PM||||I don't believe it is the battery but I will take a look.  I tried to start it 15 minutes after but it cranked faster, just not fast enough to start up.  Left it for half an hour and then it started up but with some effort.  I was at my girlfriend's when it happened so I decided to just go home and leave it here so I can take a look at it when I have the time.  (stupid university exam).   I got together with Mach10 and some other guys the night before and when I started, he said he could hear it not starting right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ferrari_cdn||10-08-2001||09:14 PM||||Well after leaving my car in the garage, she seems to start up ok when cold.  I guess she doesn't want to start when hot.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||10-08-2001||09:20 PM||||Hey Cdn!<BR>I would replace the starter, but add a heat shield...<BR>When they get heat soaked, they die...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||10-08-2001||10:07 PM||||I just replaced mine for the same reason.  A heatshield sounds like a good idea -- the starter gets toasted by the exhaust.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ferrari_cdn||10-08-2001||10:09 PM||||Are starters difficult/expensive to replace?||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrPBody||10-09-2001||07:43 AM||||Compared to what?<P>I think I paid US$40 for a rebuilt starter at Autozone.<P>On a difficulty scale where 1 = changing your air filter and 10 = V8 engine swap, replacing your starter rates around 3.  The hardest part is wiggling the starter around the exhaust.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||10-09-2001||08:15 AM||||Replace the starter shim if needed and use a dab of blue threadlocker on the bolt threads.  The previous owner of mine didn't, and I lost a bolt.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||10-09-2001||08:18 AM||||Does anyone rebuild there own starters anymore? <BR>Brushes $3.00,End Bushings $0.85, 30 minutes work.||||reg||5
Z||000010||Mach10||10-09-2001||05:54 PM||||Wolf: From what I've seen and heard, his windings are coming apart as well. It's not just the bushings, although they DO sound ragged.<BR>The damn thing is smoking, and it barely has any crank. The heat problem tells me that the insulation in the armature is breaking down, and it's a PITA to rewind a motor like that by hand....||||reg||1
